# Docker build context filter (local `docker build` AND the Cloud Build step behind
# `gcloud run deploy --source .`). Keep: api/ and contracts/ (fixtures, demo_products,
# kb_index.json). Everything else is either the iOS app, docs, caches or secrets.
# Debug: `docker build --no-cache --progress=plain .` and look at the "transferring context" size.

# --- iOS app (developed separately; never shipped to Cloud Run) ---
Pear
Pear.xcodeproj
contracts/swift
**/*.xcodeproj
**/xcuserdata
**/DerivedData

# --- VCS / tooling ---
.git
.github
.claude
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# --- Python caches and envs ---
api/.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# --- docs, infra, local-only files ---
docs
infra
Makefile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.gcloudignore

# --- secrets: never in the image (plan 7.9) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.plist
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
**/*service-account*.json
**/*-key.json
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
